=== empirical Fuseki dataset probes against the real live instance (informed the adapter design) ===
GET /$/ping -> HTTP 200 (already known from verify_external_services.py)
GET /ocor/sparql?query=SELECT+*+WHERE+{?s+?p+?o} without an Accept header -> HTTP 200 but SPARQL-XML results (not JSON); first test run failed json.JSONDecodeError on this response shape -- fixed by sending Accept: application/sparql-results+json explicitly on every query
POST /ocor/update (SPARQL 1.1 Update, Content-Type: application/sparql-update) -> HTTP 204, real insert/delete verified round-trip against the live in-memory 'ocor' dataset (infra/fuseki/Dockerfile's CMD ["--mem", "/ocor"])
GET /$/datasets (Fuseki admin API) -> HTTP 403 'only localhost access allowed' through the container's published port; not needed since the pre-configured /ocor dataset's query/update endpoints work directly

